+/*
+ * Kernir patch 0014: read_Header copies the whole kName block (every
+ * entry name, UTF-16LE, NUL-terminated) before the first header is
+ * returned, so the caller cannot stop a crafted block in time. A name
+ * over KERNIR_7Z_NAME_UNITS UTF-16 units is refused while the block is
+ * copied: UTF-8 takes at least one byte per unit, so such a name is
+ * over the 64 KiB a Kernir entry name may hold. A block over
+ * KERNIR_7Z_NAMES_BYTES plus each name's 2-byte terminator is refused
+ * before anything is copied: UTF-16 takes at most 2 bytes per UTF-8
+ * byte, so such names hold more than the 256 MiB of UTF-8 names (and
+ * link targets) Kernir lists per archive. Both return
+ * KERNIR_7Z_REFUSED with the error set.
